## **Summary: __sync_meta Flow**

| Stage | File | Handling | Filtering |
|-------|------|----------|-----------|
| **Write** | `sync_meta.rs::write_sync_meta_entry()` | Direct Loro map insert → triggers observer | None |
| **Observe** | `loro_observer.rs::setup_layer_observer()` | Loro observer captures delta + ops | UI notifications blocked |
| **Broadcast** | `broadcast.rs::broadcast_update()` | Same as regular layers | None (full broadcast) |
| **Transfer** | `sync/protocol.rs::on_sync_offer()` | 3-step protocol (SyncOffer/Accept/Ack) | None (standard protocol) |
| **Apply** | `apply.rs::handle_apply_update()` | CRDT merge + `process_creator_sync_meta()` on node | Node-side only processes |
| **Distribution** | `sync_meta.rs::process_creator_sync_meta()` | Reads entries, writes to other peers' __sync_meta | Open/Explicit grants |
| **Subscribe** | `subscription.rs::bootstrap_sync_meta()` | Peer added as subscriber to own __sync_meta | Added like any layer |
| **Pull** | `subscribe.rs::check_sync_meta_and_subscribe()` | Query unsynced, send LayerSubscribe | User mode only |
| **Delivery** | `subscribe.rs::on_layer_subscribe_ack()` | Decrypt, apply, mark synced | Full validation |

**Key Points**:
1. **`__sync_meta` IS broadcast like regular layers** (broadcast_update processes it identically)
2. **`__sync_meta` SKIPS UI notifications** (filtered in observer)
3. **`__sync_meta` goes through same 3-step sync protocol** (SyncOffer/Accept/Ack)
4. **Node-side processes __sync_meta entries** to distribute discovery (process_creator_sync_meta)
5. **Peer-side pulls new layers** via LayerSubscribe after __sync_meta update arrives
6. **Entry marked synced** when node exports layer snapshot in LayerSubscribeAck

